7%. THREE DEFECTS: (1) NUMERIC BASELINE -- 'With the tower form E_0^full active, the framework-derived value overshoots the calibrated value by +1.75%'. Against the CALIBRATED value defined three paragraphs earlier (4.179) the overshoot is +1.16%; +1.75% is the overshoot against the TYPED-crossings value 4.155, which the block introduces only as a parenthetical alternative. Proposed: name the baseline. (2) ORDERING -- the table lists CAL-1 = m_e first and CAL-2 = m_mu/m_e second, but the prose immediately below says 'The first input is a dimensionless ratio -- it fixes q_0' and 'The second input sets the leptonic mass scale', i.e. the reverse. (3) ABSOLUTE-MASS EXCISION (2026-08-11) -- the Predictions list carries 'Muon mass', 'Proton mass: via Skein pair formula ...' and 'Neutron mass: m_n = m_p + Q_beta' as predictions from q_0 + m_e. Absolute masses are m_e-scaled renderings of ratios and are no longer framework predictions; the muon entry is at least self-labelled '(first prediction, by construction matches calibration input)'. Proposed: restate as m_p/m_e, m_n/m_e and the splitting Delta_pn.","history":2},{"id":"trap-performed-warmth","group":"trap","result":"pass","severity":"minor","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:r03","history":2},{"id":"trap-rhetorical-pivot","group":"trap","result":"pass","severity":"major","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:r03","history":2},{"id":"trap-superlative","group":"trap","result":"fail","severity":"minor","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:r03","notes":"proposed (structural): 'one of the two most precisely measured particle masses' or simply drop the clause -- the other two reasons carry the argument.","history":2},{"id":"trap-thesis-restatement","group":"trap","result":"pass","severity":"major","stale":true,"freshness":"st